Third-party code in src/port/rx
===============================

This folder is for Renesas RX (RXv1, RXv2 and RXv3), with GCC's rx-elf
calling convention.

The three files listed below come from picolibc, copied byte for byte and
never edited. They are Nick Clifton's, written for newlib at Red Hat. Each
carries only its copyright line, and picolibc's COPYING.picolibc puts every
file it doesn't list by name under the licence it calls Default-1, the
three-clause BSD licence, whose text is given at the end of this file. The
other files in this folder belong to libterae and are under libterae's
licence, given at the top of each: port_memcpy.S, port_memmove.S and
port_memset.S, which are the files assembled, port_memcmp.c, and
picolibc.h, an empty stand-in for picolibc's generated header.

The port_*.S files are checked by assembling them with GNU as, from
binutils built for rx-elf: see "What is checked" below.


